      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='71000' id='15' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98000' x='1000' y='800'>
            <zone h='4200' id='16' type-v2='title' w='98000' x='1000' y='800'>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone h='66800' id='7' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98000' x='1000' y='5000'>
              <zone h='66800' id='5' name='Response Curves' w='98000' x='1000' y='5000'>
                <layout-cache minheight='198' minwidth='159' type-h='scalable' type-w='scalable' />
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone h='10500' id='17' type-v2='text' w='98000' x='1000' y='88700'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This chart shows how the simulated ground rupture responds as an earthquake grows. The horizontal axis is the driver — either the amount of fault slip or the equivalent earthquake magnitude — and the vertical axis is one feature of the resulting rupture: the height of the step, the width of the disturbed zone, the tilt of the scarp, or the net displacement. The faint points are individual simulated trials; each bold line is the fitted trend for one condition, summarizing the cloud beneath it.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>The three controls drive everything. </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' italic='true'>Driver</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> sets what&apos;s on the horizontal axis, </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' italic='true'>Response</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> sets which rupture feature is measured, and </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' italic='true'>Condition By</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> splits the trials into groups — by geological style of the break, fault steepness, soil strength, and so on — drawing one trend line per group. Comparing those lines shows which conditions produce more severe rupture for the same amount of slip, and how sensitive each response is to the driver.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h='16900' id='8' name='Response Curves' pane-specification-id='0' param='[federated.1or8g8o1xpy8wd1a368cu1icvhuo].[none:Calculation_5561481034330115:nk]' type-v2='color' w='49000' x='1000' y='71800'>
